WEBVTT

01:03.938 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:06.066 --> 01:07.150
EMERGENCY ROOM

01:21.706 --> 01:23.208
Actually,

01:24.417 --> 01:26.461
I used to live in that room
a few years ago.

01:27.128 --> 01:29.506
The window frame was a bit warped,

01:29.589 --> 01:32.967
so fortunately,
I think it allowed a lot of ventilation.

01:35.887 --> 01:37.806
Goodness, what if I'd missed it?

01:38.473 --> 01:40.725
What if I had missed the flight?

01:40.809 --> 01:42.393
For some reason, I wanted to come.

01:42.477 --> 01:43.812
I just wanted to come.

01:45.522 --> 01:47.524
You saved her, ma'am.

01:47.607 --> 01:48.608
No.

01:49.317 --> 01:51.528
Geum-myeong saved me.

01:53.488 --> 01:56.241
Our Geum-myeong is much kinder than I am,

01:56.825 --> 01:58.493
so she went easy on me.

01:59.744 --> 02:01.871
I really can't go on.

02:03.081 --> 02:04.666
I really can't go on anymore.

02:10.839 --> 02:14.342
You have to stay healthy
so you can keep Geum-myeong safe.

02:15.885 --> 02:16.761
Oh my.

02:18.138 --> 02:18.972
By the way,

02:19.681 --> 02:22.517
are you the landlord's son-in-law?

02:23.309 --> 02:25.061
Well, actually…

02:31.818 --> 02:32.652
He's…

02:33.236 --> 02:35.238
That's Park Geum-myeong's son.

02:35.321 --> 02:36.197
Huh?

02:37.532 --> 02:39.159
You know Park Geum-myeong's son?

02:39.242 --> 02:40.076
Sorry?

02:40.952 --> 02:44.122
Well, I didn't know whose son he was.

02:57.093 --> 02:57.927
Give me that.

03:00.096 --> 03:01.014
What…

03:11.983 --> 03:13.735
Am I a maid dating a prince?

03:14.736 --> 03:16.779
You. I choose you. You.

03:16.863 --> 03:18.907
Hey, keep your voice down.

03:19.407 --> 03:21.117
Why are you bringing that up here?

03:21.201 --> 03:22.869
Let's just get married. Okay?

03:22.952 --> 03:24.537
Let's just get it done already!

03:24.621 --> 03:26.581
Hey, my mom's here.

03:31.336 --> 03:34.297
Hey, kick them out
and tell them to play elsewhere.

03:34.380 --> 03:36.174
Goodness, she's all grown up.

03:39.052 --> 03:39.886
Excuse me.

03:40.553 --> 03:41.888
Have you done this yet?

03:42.889 --> 03:44.140
Right.

03:46.643 --> 03:49.145
Why take the ring
if you're gonna do whatever you want?

03:49.229 --> 03:51.898
You took the ring, so that's it.
It's a done deal!

03:53.691 --> 03:56.694
Don't go. Marry me.
You have the ring on, so that's it.

03:58.571 --> 04:01.699
Where did she manage to find
the exact same type?

04:02.283 --> 04:03.284
I told you to move.

04:03.368 --> 04:06.204
-I don't feel well.
-I told you I didn't like that area.

04:06.287 --> 04:08.248
Have you ever inhaled gas?

04:08.331 --> 04:11.209
The doctor said being nagged
would give me more headaches.

04:11.292 --> 04:13.753
So why should you be inhaling gas?

04:14.379 --> 04:18.466
Let's just get married and live
in an apartment with an oil boiler.

04:18.549 --> 04:22.971
Who proposes with an oil boiler
instead of a diamond?

04:23.054 --> 04:26.391
Dear me, they're just talking on and on
without any shame.

04:26.474 --> 04:28.434
Am I asking for something extraordinary?

04:28.935 --> 04:30.895
They don't even replace the streetlights.

04:30.979 --> 04:32.897
I hate that you go up and down alone.

04:33.690 --> 04:35.858
You shouldn't be able
to see your breath in your bedroom.

04:35.942 --> 04:37.944
I hate that you live in a place like that.

04:38.027 --> 04:40.947
That you don't sleep enough
'cause you sell late-night tickets.

04:41.030 --> 04:43.324
I hate that we can't call
because of your landlord!

04:44.158 --> 04:47.537
Why do you do everything by yourself?
Ye-rim and Min-seon don't.

04:47.620 --> 04:48.454
Who else…

04:49.330 --> 04:50.415
Who else…

04:53.209 --> 04:54.752
Don't you watch the news?

04:55.253 --> 04:58.548
In the blink of an eye,
you can get in an accident and die.

04:58.631 --> 05:00.675
What if you died alone from inhaling gas?

05:02.593 --> 05:04.429
What if you die from something bad?

05:04.929 --> 05:06.889
But I didn't die.

05:10.476 --> 05:12.520
-How could I live?
-Come on.

05:13.313 --> 05:17.942
You're still like this
even after the army?

05:18.526 --> 05:20.361
Did you really finish your service?

05:20.445 --> 05:21.696
If you die,

05:21.779 --> 05:22.613
I'll die.

05:23.656 --> 05:25.783
That's all I thought about in the taxi.

05:25.867 --> 05:26.743
Hey.

05:27.368 --> 05:29.078
Life goes on for the living.

05:29.162 --> 05:30.955
So you'd live if I died?

05:31.497 --> 05:33.958
I mean, barely…

05:34.042 --> 05:36.502
I'd barely get by.

05:41.507 --> 05:42.383
Stop smiling.

05:45.845 --> 05:47.263
You're so cute.

05:48.389 --> 05:50.266
So annoying!

05:50.767 --> 05:54.354
I just inhaled a tiny bit of gas,
just a tiny bit.

05:54.437 --> 05:56.606
You know my little nostrils, right?

05:56.689 --> 05:59.317
I can't inhale much with these.

06:04.197 --> 06:05.198
Geum-myeong.

06:05.948 --> 06:07.492
Please don't be alone.

06:08.201 --> 06:09.035
Please?

06:10.453 --> 06:11.788
You'll be marrying me.

06:12.663 --> 06:14.624
You won't be marrying my mother.

06:16.584 --> 06:19.629
I really will
do something about my family.

06:20.129 --> 06:22.673
Ae-sun will be living with me,
not my grandmother.

06:23.508 --> 06:25.093
I'll keep Ae-sun safe from her.

06:25.593 --> 06:28.179
I'll do whatever it takes
to handle my family.

06:28.805 --> 06:31.682
You just need to get on
my mom's good side from now on.

06:31.766 --> 06:32.809
Why should I?

06:33.434 --> 06:34.936
I don't like your mom either.

06:36.854 --> 06:39.399
My mother is soft at heart.

06:39.482 --> 06:42.485
If she's so softhearted,
how could she say that to my face?

06:47.073 --> 06:48.157
Say what to your face?

06:48.241 --> 06:50.827
Oh my God, you scared me.

06:51.661 --> 06:52.495
Hello, Mother.

06:52.578 --> 06:55.289
Does your mother disapprove
of my daughter?

06:56.207 --> 06:58.876
No, Mom. That's not what we meant--

06:58.960 --> 07:00.962
Why would she? Why?

07:16.853 --> 07:18.771
I can't believe what I'm seeing.

07:21.941 --> 07:24.110
Are you really Sang-gil's daughter?

07:24.193 --> 07:25.027
Yeah.

07:26.446 --> 07:27.947
This is hilarious.

07:28.614 --> 07:30.616
What's so funny
about her being his daughter?

07:30.700 --> 07:31.868
What a devoted daughter.

07:31.951 --> 07:33.953
You must be fulfilling
your father's wishes.

07:34.036 --> 07:36.414
Enough with your yapping.

07:36.497 --> 07:40.209
Your mom and dad also sat across
from each other at that exact spot.

07:40.293 --> 07:42.670
-Hey.
-Back when this was a café.

07:42.753 --> 07:44.422
-There was coffee on the table.
-Hey!

07:44.505 --> 07:48.551
They were set up on a date.
You two came so close to being siblings.

07:49.093 --> 07:51.220
Ae-sun will kill you now.

07:52.138 --> 07:54.098
What are you, Romeo and Juliet?

07:54.182 --> 07:56.350
-So who's the winner?
-Just a bit unpolished.

07:56.434 --> 07:58.603
The winner for the final week
of December is…

07:58.686 --> 08:04.650
Whether this grand first love would become
a love song or a break-up song…

08:04.734 --> 08:06.611
The winner for the final week is…

08:07.778 --> 08:09.947
…I didn't know back then.

08:10.698 --> 08:13.367
I was just blazing with love
without any shame.

08:13.993 --> 08:16.370
What doesn't she like about Geum-myeong?

08:16.454 --> 08:18.039
No, it's not like that, Mother.

08:18.789 --> 08:20.791
Ms. Yang Geum-myeong's guardian.

08:23.586 --> 08:25.463
-Me?
-Aren't you filling it out?

08:25.546 --> 08:27.465
We need her guardian's signature.

08:27.548 --> 08:29.050
Her guardian would be…

08:29.133 --> 08:31.761
You rushed in
with her on your back earlier.

08:32.470 --> 08:33.304
Who are you?

08:37.767 --> 08:39.769
-Who are you and why--
-You know what?

08:40.770 --> 08:41.729
Same here.

08:45.316 --> 08:46.817
I don't like you either.

08:48.027 --> 08:49.403
Tell me if they dated or not.

08:49.487 --> 08:52.823
Just tell me yes or no.
You're just messing with me, aren't you?

08:53.866 --> 08:56.369
Are you sure you won't tell your father?

08:56.953 --> 09:00.748
I won't fall for it. Where's that tiger
you said you had at home?

09:01.457 --> 09:03.376
Then just forget it.

09:03.459 --> 09:06.587
Shut your mouth!
Some things are better left unsaid.

09:09.632 --> 09:11.092
They didn't date.

09:14.845 --> 09:16.681
But they did consider marriage.

09:43.124 --> 09:44.125
Was that funny?

09:47.169 --> 09:49.505
You don't think that was funny?

09:55.177 --> 09:56.971
THREE AUNTIES'
FRESHLY PICKED BY HAENYEO

10:15.573 --> 10:19.035
Aren't you going to fix your mop?
You off to a farm or what?

10:19.118 --> 10:20.161
Father.

10:21.495 --> 10:22.538
Are you happy?

10:22.622 --> 10:24.832
Do you think your hair looks cool?

10:25.583 --> 10:28.294
Just shave your head.
I'll give you 50,000 won if you do.

10:40.640 --> 10:41.641
THIS IS NOT TRASH

10:41.724 --> 10:44.185
THIS IS MY PRIDE I'VE THROWN AWAY FOR YOU

10:44.268 --> 10:45.478
COME BACK TO ME, YEM

10:47.271 --> 10:49.398
HYEON-SUK LOVES YOU FOEVER

10:50.983 --> 10:53.110
26 MONTHS OR 26 YEARS
I PROMISE I WILL WAIT

11:02.787 --> 11:05.539
Do they really not hit people
in the army anymore?

11:05.623 --> 11:09.585
-Did Cheol-yong tell you that?
-Why come along if you're gonna cry?

11:09.669 --> 11:10.586
Seriously.

11:12.421 --> 11:14.882
You should've just gone to college.

11:15.925 --> 11:19.428
This year, the College Scholastic Test
replaces the Academic Ability Exam,

11:19.512 --> 11:22.056
causing ongoing confusion for students.

11:22.139 --> 11:25.267
The new exam focuses on reasoning
rather than memorization.

11:25.351 --> 11:28.896
This has increased the number
of students falling behind.

11:28.979 --> 11:31.273
How can they expect kids
who can't walk to run?

11:31.357 --> 11:34.944
If they change things randomly,
how will the fools get into college?

11:37.154 --> 11:38.489
The army?

11:38.572 --> 11:39.949
He left suddenly.

11:40.449 --> 11:44.286
Wait, he hasn't been to the army yet?

11:44.370 --> 11:46.789
He looks like he's been
to the Korean War, right?

11:47.331 --> 11:49.583
But it turned out our Picasso was 28.

11:51.001 --> 11:52.920
The soju and popcorn are for the boss,

11:53.421 --> 11:56.006
and we can take anything else we want.

11:56.090 --> 11:56.924
The popcorn too?

11:58.050 --> 12:01.762
Is someone stopping him or something?
Why did he leave without a word?

12:01.846 --> 12:03.514
I can't eat all of this.

12:03.597 --> 12:05.975
-It's too much.
-We've known each other for years.

12:06.559 --> 12:09.729
Now that you're leaving, too,
you two won't see each other again.

12:10.229 --> 12:12.606
Still, we might run into…

12:12.690 --> 12:13.816
You won't see him.

12:13.899 --> 12:16.569
Maybe in the next life, not in this one.

12:17.153 --> 12:20.740
They say you need countless lifetimes
of fate to meet even once in this life.

12:21.365 --> 12:25.578
If you miss it when it brushes past,
that's the end.

12:39.216 --> 12:41.927
But he rushed in with me on his back.

12:42.720 --> 12:45.347
NEVER LET YOUR GUARD DOWN
NEVER LET THEM OUT OF YOUR SIGHT

12:45.431 --> 12:47.558
AND NEVER FALL IN LOVE
THE BODYGUARD

12:49.101 --> 12:51.228
People from Seoul are heartless.

13:03.824 --> 13:06.243
In the year all of my windows
swayed like waves…

13:19.465 --> 13:22.968
The 1993 KBS Korean Music Awards.

13:24.762 --> 13:25.763
The grand prize.

13:29.016 --> 13:30.518
Kim Soo-hee for "Sad Love"!

13:32.895 --> 13:34.897
…Kim Soo-hee beat Seo Taiji.

13:35.439 --> 13:38.484
The fall storm beat the spring frenzy.

13:38.984 --> 13:44.907
The eventful year of 1993
is finally coming to a close.

13:45.616 --> 13:49.078
Who could withstand the storm
that blows within one's fist-sized heart?

13:49.578 --> 13:51.872
Don't you recognize me?

13:59.547 --> 14:01.382
Fall was fall.

14:12.351 --> 14:13.477
Spring was spring.

14:15.938 --> 14:18.399
How am I supposed to sell this?

14:20.317 --> 14:22.570
So it was a season
where the wind never rested.

14:25.906 --> 14:28.534
At least I'd like to think so.

14:29.660 --> 14:32.079
And so it was a life
where the heart never settled.

14:38.043 --> 14:39.587
Though I'm poor

14:40.087 --> 14:42.506
I loved the beautiful Natasha

14:43.591 --> 14:46.051
So tonight, the snow whumps down

14:46.719 --> 14:48.512
You saw that too.

14:50.014 --> 14:52.224
Did you write that
because you like the poem?

14:54.059 --> 14:54.894
No, I just…

14:56.145 --> 14:58.022
You have a girlish sentiment.

15:03.652 --> 15:04.486
You know,

15:05.446 --> 15:09.033
a poem can even make
poverty seem picturesque.

15:09.742 --> 15:12.453
There's nothing cool about being broke,

15:13.203 --> 15:15.205
but poetry makes it seem somewhat cool.

15:17.041 --> 15:17.958
Well,

15:19.251 --> 15:20.502
things like painting…

15:22.171 --> 15:23.881
I couldn't paint even if I wanted to.

15:27.593 --> 15:29.345
Making money off your talent

15:30.596 --> 15:32.556
is something not everyone can do.

15:33.307 --> 15:34.391
So,

15:35.434 --> 15:37.978
Mr. Park Toto, you're not poor,

15:38.646 --> 15:42.483
and more importantly,
that Natasha of yours isn't beautiful.

15:43.734 --> 15:45.778
Don't hang back for no reason.

15:47.529 --> 15:48.822
I'm not sure

15:48.906 --> 15:52.034
if this will help you get over her.

15:54.411 --> 15:58.415
Your Natasha,
without makeup, is just a donkey.

16:02.336 --> 16:03.170
You know…

16:06.298 --> 16:07.299
my mom asked

16:07.967 --> 16:10.219
if you're planning to take the TOEFL.

16:15.432 --> 16:16.934
She has… books for you.

16:35.786 --> 16:39.331
If you keep pitying yourself
and saying your life sucks,

16:39.415 --> 16:41.000
your life will really suck.

16:41.709 --> 16:44.211
If you think you're only worth 100 won,

16:44.294 --> 16:46.672
who would think you're worth 1,000 won?

16:46.755 --> 16:49.675
Stop pitying yourself

16:50.175 --> 16:53.429
and say something sweet to yourself
so you can stand tall.

16:54.346 --> 16:56.473
You're hunched
like Master Roshi right now.

16:57.433 --> 16:58.851
Do you read Dragon Ball?

16:59.435 --> 17:01.645
Honestly, it's a good thing
you're not family.

17:02.146 --> 17:07.317
If you were my little brother, my God,
I'd give your back a good beating.

17:10.029 --> 17:11.530
You do know how to laugh.

17:12.656 --> 17:14.825
Yeah, I didn't know I could either.

17:27.463 --> 17:28.839
This is that tree, right?

17:35.471 --> 17:37.014
The biggest tree in Korea.

17:39.641 --> 17:43.020
I chose this place
because of that thing up there.

17:43.103 --> 17:46.398
Up there, you'll see
the biggest Christmas tree in Korea.

17:47.107 --> 17:47.941
Wow.

17:49.985 --> 17:53.572
We really have seen each other
in so many embarrassing situations.

17:56.408 --> 17:57.785
Ms. Yang, you're like

17:58.786 --> 18:00.120
a Christmas tree.

18:02.623 --> 18:05.918
A tree just does its job
no matter where you put it.

18:07.711 --> 18:08.921
What's its job?

18:10.255 --> 18:12.883
Whether a Christmas tree
is in a room in a basement

18:13.759 --> 18:16.011
or a corner store no one visits…

18:18.180 --> 18:19.515
it's always sparkling.

18:21.350 --> 18:23.185
It always makes your heart pound.

18:26.480 --> 18:28.398
I just said it since it's today.

18:29.608 --> 18:30.484
I just wanted

18:31.527 --> 18:33.320
to say something sweet to you.

18:41.995 --> 18:43.789
Are you leaving or something?

18:59.638 --> 19:02.307
MY LOVE BY MY SIDE

19:09.398 --> 19:12.609
MY LOVE BY MY SIDE
DAVICHI

19:21.827 --> 19:22.953
Student passenger.

19:23.036 --> 19:28.041
This stop is Neung-dong Intersection.

19:29.918 --> 19:34.506
Ma'am. This is Neung-dong Intersection.
This is your stop!

19:56.612 --> 19:59.615
There was a time
when people held their heads up.

20:05.204 --> 20:07.831
A time when people stayed true
to their hearts.

20:07.915 --> 20:08.999
KIM HYUN-SIK BEST HITS

20:09.082 --> 20:13.712
A time when we looked at each other,
not our cell phones.

20:18.425 --> 20:19.509
Do you like it?

20:19.593 --> 20:20.677
I do.

20:20.761 --> 20:22.804
When did you record all this?

20:23.639 --> 20:26.850
-You like Kim Hyun-sik more than me.
-It was a joke.

20:38.237 --> 20:39.112
Is work tough?

20:39.947 --> 20:41.031
Is it not fun?

20:43.200 --> 20:45.452
Who goes to work for fun?

20:45.953 --> 20:47.371
People go for the money.

20:49.039 --> 20:50.791
Are you taking the bar exam for fun?

20:52.042 --> 20:52.876
Still.

20:53.835 --> 20:55.921
Wasn't there something you wanted to do?

20:57.464 --> 20:59.258
An office job wasn't your dream, right?

21:03.220 --> 21:05.847
I've also had a dream for a long time.

21:08.684 --> 21:09.601
Being independent.

21:11.478 --> 21:13.272
Living an independent life

21:15.148 --> 21:17.609
is actually quite a feat.

21:19.987 --> 21:22.531
We constantly struggled to be independent.

21:23.031 --> 21:26.410
From college entrance and graduation
to meeting the in-laws,

21:27.703 --> 21:30.539
life has been a series
of parental summons.

21:32.374 --> 21:34.876
Let's go. Tell them I won't give her away.

21:36.503 --> 21:40.173
They're almost here.
The traffic is really bad in Seoul.

21:40.257 --> 21:41.925
We even took a plane to get here.

21:43.135 --> 21:45.345
He should've brought his parents earlier.

21:46.513 --> 21:48.473
Just how bad is the traffic?

21:51.310 --> 21:52.144
Geum-myeong.

21:52.644 --> 21:54.062
Why are you fussing?

21:54.146 --> 21:56.273
You told me not to be like that.

21:56.356 --> 21:57.816
Call it.

21:58.650 --> 22:00.819
Don't be like that. Don't be.

22:00.902 --> 22:01.903
Call this off.

22:10.203 --> 22:12.080
Oh, you must have waited a long time!

22:12.164 --> 22:14.041
The traffic around here was terrible.

22:14.124 --> 22:15.000
Welcome.

22:20.797 --> 22:22.924
The traffic was terrible, wasn't it?

22:23.008 --> 22:25.594
I hope the traffic didn't
make you feel carsick. Did it?

22:26.261 --> 22:28.555
Daughter was awkwardly polite that day.

22:28.638 --> 22:29.681
We're late.

22:29.765 --> 22:32.601
It's okay. It's completely fine.

22:33.226 --> 22:37.773
Mom was the first to say it was okay
to someone who didn't even apologize.

22:38.815 --> 22:41.568
That was how
the law of gravity worked in that room.

22:41.651 --> 22:44.488
I believe we've met before.
I'm Park Geum-myeong.

22:49.576 --> 22:53.914
That day was the first time I saw
how my dad shook hands.

22:54.623 --> 22:55.582
I'm Yang Gwan-sik,

22:56.833 --> 22:58.168
Geum-myeong's father.

23:02.547 --> 23:04.966
No parents can win
against their child, right?

23:05.050 --> 23:06.635
I told her off.

23:07.469 --> 23:09.554
If they're doing it,
just get it done quickly.

23:09.638 --> 23:11.932
Dragging out a relationship
is unforgivable.

23:12.015 --> 23:13.850
It's all at the girl's expense, isn't it?

23:14.351 --> 23:16.061
Yeong-beom isn't in a hurry, is he?

23:17.854 --> 23:18.939
-Listen--
-Father.

23:19.022 --> 23:19.856
Right.

23:21.316 --> 23:24.361
We'd rather they get married
so he could just call her "wife."

23:24.945 --> 23:29.116
It must be odd for my son
to call his girlfriend "Geum-myeong"

23:29.199 --> 23:30.784
since it's my name too.

23:31.451 --> 23:33.954
That name just doesn't sit right with me.

23:39.000 --> 23:40.043
Help yourselves.

23:42.963 --> 23:45.924
I shouldn't have. I really shouldn't.

23:51.430 --> 23:53.640
A child definitely does
what it saw growing up.

24:01.648 --> 24:02.482
Let's eat.

24:04.943 --> 24:06.862
Aren't you serving the scorched rice soup?

24:08.697 --> 24:10.240
I should've shown

24:11.032 --> 24:13.285
only precious things to my precious child.

24:13.785 --> 24:15.871
Here, have some steamed fish.

24:15.954 --> 24:19.708
My heart sank as I realized
that I was a mirror for my child.

24:19.791 --> 24:21.001
The ribs here are great.

24:28.133 --> 24:31.928
Yes, so we'll choose a few dates
for the wedding in Jeju and…

24:32.012 --> 24:33.263
Did you not tell them?

24:36.558 --> 24:37.726
Why look at Yeong-beom?

24:38.852 --> 24:40.604
Mother, as I told you already--

24:40.687 --> 24:43.815
It's a little embarrassing for us

24:43.899 --> 24:45.400
to have two weddings.

24:45.484 --> 24:48.695
There's no need to go down there
and make Yeong-beom play the monkey.

24:49.738 --> 24:52.616
I understand
the island may have its own customs,

24:52.699 --> 24:55.535
but Geum-myeong
will leave your family and join ours.

24:56.036 --> 24:58.288
So shouldn't our family come first?

25:06.671 --> 25:10.425
Anyway, let's just choose one place, then.
Would you like to have it in Jeju?

25:11.009 --> 25:12.636
Then we won't do it here.

25:13.261 --> 25:15.847
No, let's just have it in Seoul.

25:17.182 --> 25:20.018
I suppose you are finally retiring
from household duties.

25:20.852 --> 25:22.062
I doubt that.

25:22.145 --> 25:24.481
Look at how she ladled your soup.

25:25.065 --> 25:28.026
We have a long way to go, don't we?

25:29.778 --> 25:31.196
She doesn't know anything.

25:31.279 --> 25:33.990
I'm not sure if I can trust her
with a large household.

25:34.699 --> 25:35.575
Well,

25:36.743 --> 25:40.205
regarding housework,
as a working woman, it will probably be--

25:40.288 --> 25:42.624
That's why I asked her to quit her job.

25:43.875 --> 25:44.876
Didn't I?

25:45.794 --> 25:47.796
Mother, can we talk about this--

25:47.879 --> 25:49.506
Son, was I speaking to you?

25:50.674 --> 25:53.093
Give me some scorched rice soup.

25:53.760 --> 25:54.594
Sorry?

25:55.178 --> 25:56.054
Of course.

26:01.184 --> 26:04.271
Don't tell me you don't even know
how to ladle that soup.

26:06.439 --> 26:08.692
Eldest daughters normally manage fine,

26:09.484 --> 26:12.529
but Geum-myeong is a bit different.

26:12.612 --> 26:14.531
As long as she can make
a good soybean paste stew.

26:27.752 --> 26:30.046
Peas, I want some peas.

26:30.130 --> 26:32.382
Peas, here are your peas.

26:40.181 --> 26:44.603
Mom never forgot the moment
Dad turned around that day.

26:45.520 --> 26:47.397
She told me a hundred times

26:47.480 --> 26:49.899
that he was probably
the first husband in Dodong-ri

26:49.983 --> 26:51.735
to join his wife at the other table.

26:51.818 --> 26:53.820
I'll eat at this table from now on.

26:54.654 --> 26:55.488
Why?

26:55.572 --> 26:58.116
Dad chose to fight his own war.

26:58.199 --> 26:59.117
Why? You punk!

26:59.200 --> 27:02.996
He never left Mom stranded alone
on the battlefield.

27:03.496 --> 27:05.999
I also want to eat with you, Mom.

27:07.375 --> 27:08.627
Dogs are better.

27:08.710 --> 27:12.255
In those days, Dad turning around
was truly revolutionary.

27:12.756 --> 27:15.300
I realized that
as I ladled that scorched rice soup.

27:15.884 --> 27:18.511
I'll do it. I'm good at ladling too.

27:18.595 --> 27:21.097
No, just sit down.

27:21.598 --> 27:22.682
It's okay. Let me.

27:27.062 --> 27:27.896
Give it.

27:31.775 --> 27:33.985
-I can do it well.
-Please eat.

27:42.369 --> 27:44.746
Your mother does everything for you,

27:44.829 --> 27:46.665
so you don't know anything.

27:47.540 --> 27:48.541
Isn't that right?

27:53.755 --> 27:55.382
I couldn't teach her.

27:57.676 --> 27:58.968
She was so precious,

28:00.053 --> 28:01.513
too dear…

28:05.558 --> 28:08.269
so I chose not to teach her.

28:23.660 --> 28:25.995
No, I don't want to.

28:26.496 --> 28:30.834
You should give your parents a ride home.
We prefer the subway.

28:30.917 --> 28:31.751
Let's just go.

28:31.835 --> 28:33.211
Then how about a taxi?

28:33.294 --> 28:34.462
Oh, no, no.

28:34.546 --> 28:38.007
There are so many cars in Seoul.
We'll be late if there's traffic.

28:38.591 --> 28:40.093
Just take a taxi, will you?

28:43.722 --> 28:44.889
Take a taxi.

28:58.236 --> 29:00.238
You managed well today. See you.

29:01.114 --> 29:02.115
We'll go now.

29:03.158 --> 29:03.992
Bye.

29:04.826 --> 29:05.660
Bye.

29:08.204 --> 29:09.956
Mother, Father, have a safe trip home.

29:10.039 --> 29:13.376
Bye, Geum-myeong.
We'll call you when we get home.

29:13.460 --> 29:15.170
Don't worry about a thing.

29:15.253 --> 29:18.339
You do everything well. Dad knows you do.

29:18.423 --> 29:19.758
Let's go! Quickly!

29:21.092 --> 29:23.845
Bye. I'll call you when I get home.

29:24.679 --> 29:26.014
Have a safe trip, Father.

29:40.820 --> 29:42.280
My mom's crying.

29:45.158 --> 29:46.826
I messed up again, didn't I?

29:50.497 --> 29:52.415
You're so sweet.

29:53.291 --> 29:55.084
You're just such a sweet boy.

30:08.807 --> 30:09.641
My goodness.

30:10.225 --> 30:12.936
Geum-myeong,
it turns out you're an indoor plant too.

30:13.019 --> 30:14.896
-Mother.
-"Mother," what?

30:14.979 --> 30:17.816
You interrupt me
every time I open my mouth now.

30:17.899 --> 30:20.485
Why didn't you stick up for her more
in front of them?

30:20.568 --> 30:22.987
Would it kill you to stay quiet for once?

30:25.990 --> 30:28.660
What did I say
to make her tremble like that?

30:28.743 --> 30:29.828
Too precious to teach?

30:30.537 --> 30:34.040
She said that to mess with me.
Even if they begged, I'd be fuming.

30:34.123 --> 30:35.834
-Mother!
-What?

30:39.212 --> 30:40.046
Mother,

30:40.964 --> 30:41.798
the thing is…

30:44.801 --> 30:45.802
I am an indoor plant.

30:45.885 --> 30:46.886
What was that?

30:47.679 --> 30:48.513
I also grew up

30:49.931 --> 30:52.559
in an unbelievably safe greenhouse,

30:53.977 --> 30:56.145
treated as the most precious thing.

30:57.272 --> 30:58.231
So…

31:00.441 --> 31:03.444
please stop being so harsh to me.

31:06.698 --> 31:08.449
It'll make my mom and dad cry.

31:11.828 --> 31:12.787
Good God.

31:22.213 --> 31:24.799
Did I send her to college
to make soybean paste stew?

31:24.883 --> 31:28.761
She acts like she's so great around me.
Why couldn't she say a word there?

31:30.889 --> 31:32.098
Why did you do that?

31:36.686 --> 31:38.104
You couldn't stand it?

31:41.357 --> 31:43.109
Our Geum-myeong has parents.

31:43.192 --> 31:44.485
She has her family!

31:45.445 --> 31:48.239
So that's what you wanted her to know?

31:48.990 --> 31:50.408
You were holding back well.

31:51.326 --> 31:54.078
I thought you'd throw a fit
and refuse to give your girl away.

31:54.704 --> 31:57.165
I wanted to,
hundreds, maybe thousands of times.

31:57.248 --> 31:59.375
But she says she likes him.

32:00.710 --> 32:04.756
I held back because calling it off
might make our baby hurt.

32:05.256 --> 32:07.759
It's not because she's any less than him.

32:08.259 --> 32:11.429
I want to do everything for her marriage.

32:12.013 --> 32:15.934
I won't let anyone say my child
couldn't even bring a silver spoon.

32:17.018 --> 32:18.436
Our Geum-myeong has parents.

32:19.979 --> 32:21.105
Both Mom and Dad.

32:25.985 --> 32:28.029
Do it. Do it all.

32:30.782 --> 32:33.284
I was the boss at my house

32:34.160 --> 32:35.787
but just a minion in theirs.

32:35.870 --> 32:37.622
I told you we should take a taxi!

32:38.706 --> 32:41.459
My mother-in-law really hates waiting.
Seriously!

32:42.251 --> 32:44.545
Is she trying to make me mad, or what?

32:44.629 --> 32:45.922
Come on, run!

32:46.005 --> 32:47.799
What is she, your master?

32:47.882 --> 32:49.592
We have to cross now!

32:49.676 --> 32:52.053
-I'm not going.
-Mom, come on!

32:52.136 --> 32:54.055
I told you my feet hurt, didn't I?

32:54.138 --> 32:56.099
I told you we should take a taxi,
didn't I?

32:56.891 --> 32:59.018
Is she waiting
with a stopwatch or something?

32:59.102 --> 33:01.104
So what if we're a little late?

33:01.187 --> 33:04.565
They kept us waiting for an hour
at our first meeting, didn't they?

33:05.149 --> 33:08.111
Come on, Mom! What is wrong with you?

33:08.194 --> 33:10.571
Did you do something wrong?
Do you owe them money?

33:11.239 --> 33:13.366
You act like you're the boss at home.

33:14.575 --> 33:16.119
Aren't you the boss at our home?

33:16.202 --> 33:17.370
Be a minion there,

33:17.453 --> 33:20.039
and Mom and Dad
become the lowest of minions!

33:22.875 --> 33:25.169
It's so pretty. You look beautiful.

33:26.462 --> 33:28.923
You look so good in pink, you know.

33:29.007 --> 33:30.341
Like you're in your thirties.

33:30.425 --> 33:32.927
There's no way
I look like I'm in my thirties.

33:33.011 --> 33:33.845
No way.

33:35.054 --> 33:36.556
Let's go with pink, then.

33:37.682 --> 33:40.435
We had another shade of pink.

33:42.437 --> 33:45.106
Why did you come
if you're not going to help me choose?

33:47.233 --> 33:48.067
Well…

33:50.445 --> 33:51.279
What?

33:53.239 --> 33:54.323
Won't you add flowers?

33:55.324 --> 33:56.701
Flowers? No need.

33:56.784 --> 33:59.454
You should add floral embroidery
to the pink.

34:00.496 --> 34:01.456
I'm just worried

34:02.248 --> 34:04.250
I might come off as over the top.

34:04.333 --> 34:06.377
Do you have another daughter?

34:06.461 --> 34:09.839
This is the only time you'll sit
as the bride's mother.

34:10.506 --> 34:11.716
Do whatever you want.

34:12.383 --> 34:13.217
Well…

34:15.511 --> 34:16.471
Actually,

34:17.055 --> 34:21.517
you know
those tiny flower patterns in rows?

34:21.601 --> 34:25.688
I saw it
when Cheol-yong's brother got married.

34:27.482 --> 34:28.566
So you do want flowers.

34:28.649 --> 34:31.444
If we cover it with flowers,

34:31.527 --> 34:34.238
it will look like she's the bride.

34:34.947 --> 34:37.325
Your mom is actually quite young, right?

34:39.118 --> 34:41.370
Go with the previous one.
The red bean soup color.

34:41.454 --> 34:43.331
But, ma'am,

34:43.831 --> 34:46.167
pink is so much better than that color.

34:47.168 --> 34:48.669
Is this your wedding?

34:48.753 --> 34:49.754
Sorry?

34:50.671 --> 34:52.173
I'll have mine with this emerald color.

34:53.674 --> 34:54.550
Mother.

34:55.718 --> 34:57.345
My mom likes pink.

34:57.428 --> 34:58.763
Pink is tacky.

34:59.847 --> 35:01.974
It's not just your guests
who will be attending.

35:04.060 --> 35:06.395
What a relief that we came here together.

35:06.479 --> 35:07.313
A huge relief.

35:23.121 --> 35:25.915
You kept turning it down,

35:26.874 --> 35:28.501
so I'd like to…

35:31.003 --> 35:32.255
There's no need.

35:32.839 --> 35:34.882
Otherwise,

35:34.966 --> 35:38.928
if you could specify what you'd like,
we will--

35:39.011 --> 35:41.222
I appreciate the thought.

35:42.014 --> 35:42.849
But…

35:44.851 --> 35:46.727
why just appreciate the thought?

35:47.228 --> 35:48.771
Please don't be like that.

35:52.942 --> 35:55.736
Well, if you could just…

35:56.320 --> 35:57.363
Fine, then.

35:57.446 --> 35:58.447
I'll take it.

36:09.625 --> 36:13.796
Our Geum-myeong may not be
very gentle or soft-spoken…

36:15.882 --> 36:17.175
but she has a deep heart.

36:17.258 --> 36:19.218
She's also quite caring.

36:19.302 --> 36:20.553
So please see her

36:21.429 --> 36:22.847
in a good light.

36:23.472 --> 36:27.101
I find Yeong-beom quite… endearing.

36:28.019 --> 36:30.980
More than anything else,
my daughter likes him,

36:31.063 --> 36:34.400
and she says he really cares about her,

36:34.901 --> 36:37.111
so I've grown to like him.

36:38.487 --> 36:39.572
Mrs. Oh.

36:39.655 --> 36:40.823
Yes?

36:40.907 --> 36:44.160
I have a condition where I might die
if I don't speak my mind.

36:51.751 --> 36:53.544
Hey! Come on.

36:54.629 --> 36:57.215
Why are you so late? It's been so awkward.

36:57.298 --> 37:00.051
-Why are you out here?
-Just in case you couldn't find it.

37:01.802 --> 37:02.637
It's just them?

37:03.596 --> 37:05.264
Yes. Why?

37:05.348 --> 37:06.599
Is that a problem?

37:07.099 --> 37:09.518
Look at you. Your hair's a mess.

37:09.602 --> 37:11.062
Where is it? Which way?

37:11.145 --> 37:12.897
-It's this way. Yes.
-This way?

37:13.940 --> 37:14.774
What's wrong?

37:14.857 --> 37:18.527
Is there anything a mother wouldn't say
for her child's sake?

37:18.611 --> 37:20.905
I fear if I get dragged into this
without saying anything,

37:20.988 --> 37:23.199
I'll regret it for the rest of my life.

37:25.159 --> 37:25.993
I see.

37:26.953 --> 37:28.079
Mrs. Oh.

37:28.871 --> 37:30.373
Please stop this wedding.

37:30.957 --> 37:34.001
I've had the patience of a saint
while trying to go along with this,

37:34.085 --> 37:36.212
but as a mother, you must know, right?

37:36.837 --> 37:37.838
My Yeong-beom

37:39.006 --> 37:40.299
is my life.

37:42.009 --> 37:43.344
My masterpiece.

37:45.221 --> 37:48.766
I'm sorry to say this,
but I don't find Geum-myeong endearing.

37:49.517 --> 37:50.643
She's hard to like.

37:51.185 --> 37:53.729
Do you really have to send her
to a family like this?

37:58.442 --> 38:00.403
Let's each convince our own children.

38:00.486 --> 38:01.529
Whatever happens,

38:01.612 --> 38:04.573
let's do our very best
to stop this once and for all.

38:06.659 --> 38:07.660
Could we?

38:16.794 --> 38:18.671
What is it about Geum-myeong…

38:21.841 --> 38:23.843
that you are so displeased with?

38:46.574 --> 38:49.910
Why were you so quiet at lunch?
Do you know how uneasy Yeong-beom felt?

38:49.994 --> 38:51.120
So what if he did?

38:52.371 --> 38:53.706
Do you like him that much?

38:53.789 --> 38:54.623
What?

38:55.166 --> 38:57.043
What do you like about that boy?

38:58.085 --> 38:59.128
Don't you like him?

39:00.880 --> 39:02.631
-No. I don't like him.
-Why not?

39:04.175 --> 39:05.009
He's hard to like.

39:05.718 --> 39:07.678
Is there really
anything special about him?

39:07.762 --> 39:10.306
It's not like he passed the bar exam.

39:10.389 --> 39:13.351
He's got nothing and isn't any better, so…

39:13.434 --> 39:14.268
What about me?

39:14.352 --> 39:17.605
So what do I have?
What am I better than him at?

39:17.688 --> 39:19.648
You think I'm less than him, too,

39:19.732 --> 39:22.026
so you couldn't even say
you liked the pink hanbok.

39:22.109 --> 39:24.320
No, I would never think that!

39:24.403 --> 39:26.489
Then why didn't you say anything to her?

39:26.572 --> 39:29.325
-Why grovel before her?
-Because she might be cold to you!

39:30.326 --> 39:32.203
I held back so she wouldn't hate you,

39:32.286 --> 39:34.580
not because I thought
you were less than him.

39:35.247 --> 39:37.208
What could you be lacking? What?

39:37.792 --> 39:39.752
What a load of crap, seriously.

39:44.548 --> 39:45.383
What is it?

39:46.801 --> 39:48.552
Did Yeong-beom's mother say something?

39:54.642 --> 39:58.270
I'm worried my child will be disliked
just sending them to kindergarten.

39:58.354 --> 40:02.566
How can I act on my temper
when I'm sending you to her family?

40:02.650 --> 40:04.902
Just go ahead and act on your temper!

40:09.782 --> 40:11.242
So you'd better

40:12.576 --> 40:13.577
get it together.

40:13.661 --> 40:16.205
Get your act together for my sake.

40:16.705 --> 40:21.585
Even a small scratch on your heart
deeply bruises both mine and your dad's.

40:24.463 --> 40:26.257
I was a bad brat at my house,

40:27.633 --> 40:30.302
but a barbarian at theirs.

40:31.220 --> 40:32.972
Everything was my fault.

40:34.014 --> 40:35.099
It was you, wasn't it?

40:35.599 --> 40:39.145
I told you it was my decision.
Don't I have my own thoughts?

40:39.228 --> 40:41.647
Geum-myeong, do you have a house?

40:41.730 --> 40:42.773
Do you have money?

40:43.566 --> 40:47.403
You thought he'd get you a house
if you wheedled him into moving out?

40:47.486 --> 40:49.947
It's because you're making it hard for me.

40:50.030 --> 40:52.867
How much did you roast him
to make him act like this toward me?

40:52.950 --> 40:55.369
You've really got him under your thumb.

40:55.453 --> 40:56.745
Mother, don't you hear me?

40:56.829 --> 40:57.663
Mother.

40:58.456 --> 41:01.625
I never talked to Yeong-beom
about moving out.

41:01.709 --> 41:03.586
How sly and shameless.

41:04.670 --> 41:07.214
If I don't even flinch
when she pokes a little…

41:07.298 --> 41:08.257
Mother, go home.

41:08.924 --> 41:10.009
Who do you take after?

41:10.092 --> 41:11.760
…she'll inevitably cross the line.

41:11.844 --> 41:15.306
I thought I made myself quite clear
to your mother.

41:15.389 --> 41:18.350
Does she still insist on
becoming related to me by marriage?

41:18.976 --> 41:20.895
-Mother, just go home.
-Let go!

41:23.147 --> 41:25.649
What did you say to my mom?

41:26.650 --> 41:28.694
Your mother didn't even tell you?

41:29.445 --> 41:33.115
She must really want to force you
into our family.

41:33.199 --> 41:34.241
Mother!

41:34.325 --> 41:35.326
What did you say?

41:36.702 --> 41:38.746
I told her
we should both stop the wedding.

41:39.246 --> 41:40.539
Can't I say what I must?

41:44.418 --> 41:45.878
That big-nosed woman.

41:46.462 --> 41:48.672
All her age has gone to her nose.

41:48.756 --> 41:52.301
She's just worried
you'll make her look older and uglier.

41:52.384 --> 41:53.344
It's obvious.

41:53.427 --> 41:56.138
Why emerald for her
and red bean soup color for you?

41:56.222 --> 41:57.640
I'd be happy to wear

41:57.723 --> 42:00.476
the red bean soup-colored hanbok
a thousand times

42:00.976 --> 42:03.270
as long as she treats Geum-myeong well.

42:03.354 --> 42:05.648
Who in the world would hate Geum-myeong?

42:05.731 --> 42:08.734
She was the teachers' favorite.
Everyone ends up liking her.

42:09.235 --> 42:10.694
That elementary school teacher

42:10.778 --> 42:13.322
who'd only send Geum-myeong
to fetch coal for the furnace.

42:13.405 --> 42:14.532
That horse-faced one.

42:14.615 --> 42:17.826
Eventually, he gave her
the Good Child Award.

42:17.910 --> 42:19.912
I actually gave him an envelope.

42:21.622 --> 42:22.456
30,000 won.

42:23.374 --> 42:27.962
I never sent our kids on a picnic
with just one roll of gimbap.

42:28.045 --> 42:31.674
I always made sure to send two rolls,
one for the teacher as well.

42:33.300 --> 42:37.471
I didn't want my kids to feel lacking,
financially or emotionally.

42:38.264 --> 42:41.058
Is that why you gave her
so much money as a wedding gift?

42:41.141 --> 42:44.228
What could be more upsetting
than my child being hated?

42:45.437 --> 42:47.147
Why can't she understand that

42:47.856 --> 42:49.400
when she's a mother too?

42:49.984 --> 42:52.444
Did that big-nosed woman say something?

42:53.070 --> 42:53.904
It's just…

42:56.198 --> 42:57.366
She's too harsh.

42:57.866 --> 43:00.494
She's too harsh on Geum-myeong.

43:02.871 --> 43:05.583
Geum-myeong does everything well.
She does well on her own.

43:06.208 --> 43:07.876
What does she do well?

43:07.960 --> 43:11.422
I know from experience that walking
on eggshells only makes life miserable.

43:11.505 --> 43:12.756
Geum-myeong is different.

43:13.841 --> 43:16.635
We raised her
so she wouldn't tolerate such misery.

43:17.553 --> 43:21.098
You're set on driving a wedge
between me and my son, aren't you?

43:21.181 --> 43:24.602
I didn't say much, and you're crying?
Did you learn that from your mom too?

43:25.561 --> 43:27.354
Mother, why did you do that?

43:27.438 --> 43:29.106
How far are you going to go?

43:29.189 --> 43:31.066
Educated people don't say much.

43:31.150 --> 43:34.486
-I only said a few things with dignity--
-Mother.

43:36.614 --> 43:39.074
You've never once shown any dignity.

43:40.034 --> 43:44.038
I can imagine how you treated my mom.

43:44.121 --> 43:44.955
What?

43:45.039 --> 43:47.416
The reason I've been putting up
with you until now

43:48.542 --> 43:50.002
isn't because I'm less than him.

43:51.503 --> 43:53.922
I know how embarrassed
Yeong-beom is of you.

43:54.965 --> 43:56.925
That's the only reason I held back.

43:59.136 --> 44:01.680
He's embarrassed of me? Me?

44:02.931 --> 44:07.311
I thought your father was a lowly laborer
when I saw his hand!

44:07.394 --> 44:09.897
-Mother!
-I never found his hands embarrassing.

44:09.980 --> 44:12.358
Not a single thing about my parents
embarrasses me.

44:12.441 --> 44:14.568
Throughout the wedding preparations,

44:15.361 --> 44:16.570
our family showed

44:17.237 --> 44:19.365
far more dignity than yours.

44:21.909 --> 44:24.787
Do you think it's a done deal
because the invitations went out?

44:25.496 --> 44:28.248
If I wanted to call it off… you know?

44:29.583 --> 44:30.417
Got it?

44:37.257 --> 44:38.509
I won't do it.

44:41.804 --> 44:43.222
I can't do it.

44:48.018 --> 44:49.937
How can I get married like this?

44:50.020 --> 44:51.438
My mom and dad will cry.

44:54.942 --> 44:57.111
You're breaking off the engagement?

44:58.153 --> 45:00.489
You? You are?

45:01.073 --> 45:03.617
Please stop! Stop it!

45:03.701 --> 45:04.910
Why should I stop?

45:05.703 --> 45:07.788
You owe 80% of your life to me.

45:07.871 --> 45:11.125
You are my pride! My life!

45:11.208 --> 45:12.835
Yeong-beom's life is his.

45:15.462 --> 45:17.631
The life that you say you're living.

45:20.509 --> 45:22.010
It belongs to Yeong-beom.

45:25.389 --> 45:26.974
What is it about Geum-myeong

45:28.225 --> 45:30.602
that you are so displeased with?

45:32.479 --> 45:34.148
I'm sure she's a smart girl.

45:35.983 --> 45:37.067
But this is marriage.

45:37.943 --> 45:41.405
It should be between two similar families
to avoid trouble.

45:47.995 --> 45:50.372
I never let Geum-myeong go hungry
a day in her life.

45:50.956 --> 45:53.709
Whatever she wanted to do, I--

45:53.792 --> 45:57.755
You think she grew up without shadows
in a struggling family, don't you?

45:57.838 --> 46:00.007
But a family like that doesn't exist.

46:00.674 --> 46:03.051
In a struggling family,
shadows are bound to be cast.

46:03.552 --> 46:05.554
How could it be the same as a sunlit tree?

46:13.520 --> 46:14.855
Sorry for being so blunt.

46:18.358 --> 46:20.360
But now that I've spoken my mind,

46:21.195 --> 46:24.323
I feel like a boulder
has been lifted off my chest.

46:29.828 --> 46:30.662
Ma'am.

46:31.663 --> 46:35.292
Do you know
where you're putting that boulder down?

46:40.005 --> 46:41.799
On your son's heart.

46:44.843 --> 46:46.929
That's where you're putting it down.

47:00.734 --> 47:03.695
You're just taking your son's life
and living it as your own.

47:12.496 --> 47:14.665
Hi, my name is Pororo.

47:14.748 --> 47:16.667
Hi, Pororo.

47:17.751 --> 47:18.961
Hello, friends.

47:19.503 --> 47:21.129
Pororo, what are you doing?

47:24.633 --> 47:30.097
Pope Francis arrived in Korea
for the first time this morning.

47:30.597 --> 47:32.683
Kim Seon-hee reports from the scene.

47:33.809 --> 47:37.980
Pope Francis has arrived at Seoul Air Base
in Seongnam on a chartered plane.

47:38.063 --> 47:38.939
Of all the popes…

47:39.022 --> 47:40.440
The extreme heat intensifies,

47:40.524 --> 47:43.485
leading to a sharp rise
in heat-related conditions.

47:44.278 --> 47:47.573
The Korea Disease Control Agency
stated that since May…

48:05.215 --> 48:06.550
Are you still up?

48:08.677 --> 48:10.345
Son, don't drink too much.

48:12.723 --> 48:13.557
Good night.

48:15.309 --> 48:17.561
Please stop it. Stop.

48:18.854 --> 48:21.273
Why should I walk on eggshells around her?

48:22.357 --> 48:23.358
Why should I

48:24.276 --> 48:25.944
live like this?

48:28.238 --> 48:29.239
Please go to bed.

48:29.781 --> 48:31.992
After everything I went through
to raise you?

48:33.285 --> 48:34.995
Was it all just to see this?

48:38.707 --> 48:40.918
You've only felt sorry for yourself,
haven't you?

48:42.753 --> 48:43.754
What about me?

48:46.840 --> 48:48.967
What do you have to complain about?

48:49.593 --> 48:51.011
You're just too sensitive!

48:52.429 --> 48:53.805
I did it all for you.

48:54.598 --> 48:55.766
I lived for you.

48:56.767 --> 49:00.938
If you had married that girl,
you would've been even more unhappy.

49:04.775 --> 49:06.693
How can you do this to me?

49:08.278 --> 49:10.989
How could you humiliate me like this?

49:12.574 --> 49:14.952
You are my life.

49:16.370 --> 49:17.955
My life!

49:18.038 --> 49:19.623
It's my life.

49:20.707 --> 49:24.211
It's my disgusting life, where I've never
once had what I truly wanted.

49:27.881 --> 49:30.175
Still, it's good
that you're at least happy.

49:31.426 --> 49:32.678
You're happy, aren't you?

49:33.303 --> 49:34.137
Look.

49:36.390 --> 49:39.101
You're the only one smiling at my wedding.

49:49.027 --> 49:52.698
My first love didn't end up
as a fairy tale.

49:57.119 --> 49:57.953
Geum-myeong.

50:01.164 --> 50:01.999
Hey, wait.

50:04.584 --> 50:06.878
Did you know your mom made my mom cry?

50:09.506 --> 50:12.968
I don't even want to cry right now
because of your mom.

50:22.477 --> 50:23.603
Hello, everyone.

50:23.687 --> 50:27.607
North Korean leader Kim Il Sung
died at 2:00 a.m.

50:27.691 --> 50:30.318
With the deepest grief,

50:30.402 --> 50:33.071
we announce to the people of North Korea

50:33.572 --> 50:37.242
that our great leader,
Comrade Kim Il Sung, passed away

50:37.325 --> 50:42.330
due to sudden illness
at 2:00 a.m. on July 8, 1994.

50:42.414 --> 50:45.792
How is it
that our great leader's heart of steel,

50:46.293 --> 50:50.922
so resilient to external attacks,

50:51.006 --> 50:56.762
has truly stopped beating?

50:56.845 --> 50:59.556
Thirty-four hours
after the news of Kim Il Sung's death,

50:59.639 --> 51:01.850
at noon today,
the Pyongyang Broadcasting System…

51:01.933 --> 51:03.143
When our engagement ended…

51:03.226 --> 51:06.646
The broadcast announced
the news of Kim Il Sung's death.

51:06.730 --> 51:08.940
…I cried like a North Korean spy.

51:09.024 --> 51:10.442
It is said to be a heart attack

51:10.525 --> 51:13.862
due to a combination of fatigue
and cardiovascular disease.

51:13.945 --> 51:15.405
The North Korean broadcast also…

51:25.248 --> 51:26.249
Geum-myeong.

51:34.716 --> 51:36.927
We were together for seven years.

51:38.678 --> 51:41.348
And we spent a year breaking up.

51:41.932 --> 51:43.767
So just be a sweet son.

51:43.850 --> 51:45.143
A sweet son.

51:45.227 --> 51:48.230
You're the type
who has to be nice to everyone, right?

51:48.313 --> 51:50.107
What woman would be happy with you?

51:50.190 --> 51:53.276
Everyone is unhappy and frustrated
while you keep acting nice.

51:53.777 --> 51:55.112
Did you have to say that?

51:55.737 --> 51:58.949
We jabbed at each other,
spoke harshly to each other…

51:59.825 --> 52:03.036
Have you ever lived with me?
Give it a try before deciding.

52:03.120 --> 52:04.079
Why should I?

52:04.162 --> 52:06.414
Why should I be treated like crap
by your family?

52:09.960 --> 52:11.169
Can you live without me?

52:14.005 --> 52:15.340
-You're okay with that?
-Yeah.

52:15.423 --> 52:18.385
I'd be so happy without you.
It'd be perfect if not for you.

52:37.404 --> 52:38.905
Who asked you to hug me?

52:39.614 --> 52:41.366
…and worried sick about each other,

52:42.534 --> 52:44.744
pouring our hearts out,
leaving nothing behind.

53:09.227 --> 53:10.395
It's cold.

53:11.229 --> 53:12.230
You'll freeze to death.

53:23.241 --> 53:24.409
It's past midnight.

53:27.037 --> 53:28.830
I can still give you flowers, right?

53:29.664 --> 53:30.498
Just flowers.

53:35.587 --> 53:37.547
Why give me flowers on your birthday?

53:39.758 --> 53:40.675
A gift to myself.

53:47.265 --> 53:48.350
Aren't you cold?

53:49.059 --> 53:50.101
It's freezing.

53:53.897 --> 53:54.731
Yeong-beom.

54:00.111 --> 54:01.154
Stop it.

54:08.495 --> 54:09.746
It's exhausting.

54:10.622 --> 54:11.706
Really exhausting.

54:20.715 --> 54:21.925
Is it really over?

54:24.094 --> 54:24.928
No matter what?

54:33.770 --> 54:35.105
Don't you love me anymore?

54:35.897 --> 54:37.649
Of course I do.

54:39.359 --> 54:40.360
How can I not?

54:41.903 --> 54:44.114
I do love you deeply.

54:46.741 --> 54:48.743
But I love myself deeply too.

54:50.161 --> 54:52.038
I feel so sorry for myself…

54:54.082 --> 54:55.625
that I can't do it anymore.

54:55.709 --> 54:56.876
I'll cut off my family.

54:58.336 --> 55:00.630
-Okay?
-Who wants to live like that?

55:00.714 --> 55:03.174
If your heart aches, mine will ache too.

55:19.482 --> 55:21.318
I think if we became a family,

55:22.777 --> 55:25.447
we'd end up hating each other.

55:25.530 --> 55:27.073
I can't let you go.

55:27.615 --> 55:29.451
I just can't. What should I do?

55:34.622 --> 55:36.124
Of course you can.

55:37.667 --> 55:39.419
I always tell you this, don't I?

55:41.629 --> 55:43.298
Life goes on for the living.

55:47.927 --> 55:49.012
I'm sorry…

55:51.222 --> 55:53.224
for being so harsh at the end.

55:55.226 --> 55:56.644
I'm the one who's sorry.

55:57.937 --> 56:00.106
I was so…

56:04.569 --> 56:05.612
Thank you.

56:07.072 --> 56:08.698
To be honest…

56:12.994 --> 56:15.121
I was just grateful for everything,
Yeong-beom.

56:19.876 --> 56:22.796
I'm so glad that you're the one
who'll remember me

56:24.089 --> 56:25.382
in my twenties.

56:27.133 --> 56:28.468
Do we have to do this?

56:29.302 --> 56:30.553
Do we really have to?

56:46.069 --> 56:46.903
Come on.

56:49.197 --> 56:50.031
No.

56:52.992 --> 56:54.202
But it's our last time.

57:08.967 --> 57:10.677
I'm going to miss your scent.

57:12.262 --> 57:13.263
Still,

57:14.681 --> 57:16.766
call me if anything happens, okay?

57:18.518 --> 57:20.103
You don't have anyone in Seoul.

57:20.770 --> 57:22.188
Promise you'll call me, okay?

57:25.483 --> 57:26.317
I will.

57:27.694 --> 57:28.778
I promise.

57:31.489 --> 57:32.824
Does this mean…

57:35.326 --> 57:37.287
we'll never see each other after tomorrow?

57:38.913 --> 57:40.081
How can we?

57:42.333 --> 57:44.002
How can we not?

57:45.545 --> 57:49.382
Why can't we? It's so unfair.

57:49.466 --> 57:51.217
In Seoul, where I had no one,

57:51.718 --> 57:54.095
he was my lover,

57:54.596 --> 57:55.972
my family,

57:57.557 --> 57:58.933
and my best friend.

58:01.102 --> 58:05.732
Suddenly becoming strangers
with my closest buddy

58:06.941 --> 58:08.943
felt like the Little Prince was leaving

58:10.028 --> 58:12.238
the small planet
only the two of us lived on.

01:00:58.112 --> 01:01:03.326
"JUST GET READY AND GO,
RIDE THE MOMENT WITH ALL YOU HAVE."

01:01:10.166 --> 01:01:12.418
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
